---
layout: layout.njk
permalink: "/propose/"
pageTitle: "Propose a speaker"
eleventyComputed:
  # See `archives.njk` for why this is computed rather than a plain
  # front-matter string.
  pageDescription: "Propose yourself, or someone whose work you admire, to speak in the {{ site.title }}."
---
{% from "motif-pieces.njk" import piece, heroPieces %}
{#
  The public entry point to the proposal pipeline `tools/convener_ops/
  proposal.py` already implements: a Tally form, its webhook signed and
  verified (`proposal.verify_signature`), turned into a candidate lead by
  `to_lead` (docs/operating/operations.md, "Form relay"). `site.applyForm`
  is the same field `index.njk`'s own two "Propose a speaker" buttons used
  to link straight out to; both now point here instead, so a visitor
  reads what to expect before leaving the site, and there is exactly one
  place this page needs to change if the live form ever moves.

  Two states, and the second is not hypothetical. `site.applyForm` is
  empty while `instance/config.json` still declares a placeholder instead
  of a form address (`.eleventy.js`, mirroring
  `published.py::Identity.proposal_form_url`), and this instance declared
  `https://forms.example.test/propose` from the day the old `site.json` was folded
  into the declaration for a long time -- so the button below was a
  live call to action on a public page, pointing at nothing. It now says
  so and points to the contact section instead, which is the state a fresh
  duplicate is in too: nobody has built their form before their first
  publish.
#}
<section class="hero">
  {% if motif.pieces %}{{ heroPieces(motif) }}{% endif %}
  <div class="container hero__inner">
    <p class="hero__eyebrow">Propose a speaker</p>
    <h1 class="hero__title">Bring us <em>your</em> talk.</h1>
    <p class="hero__lede">
      Propose yourself or someone whose work you admire. Early-career
      researchers are especially welcome. A volunteer from the Editorial
      Board reads every proposal.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section container">
  {% if motif.pieces %}{{ piece(motif, "below-band") }}{% endif %}
  <header class="section__head">
    <span class="section__num">01</span>
    <span class="section__label">Before you start</span>
  </header>

  <div class="notice">
    <p class="notice__eyebrow">What to expect</p>
    <p>
      The form takes a few minutes. It asks for the speaker&rsquo;s name
      and contact details, a provisional title, a short abstract and, if
      you are proposing someone else, your own details.
    </p>
    <p>
      Nothing about the speaker is published unless the talk is selected
      and they agree.
    </p>
  </div>

  {% if site.applyForm %}
  <div class="hero__actions">
    <a class="btn btn--primary" href="{{ site.applyForm }}">Open the proposal form &rarr;</a>
  </div>
  <p class="aside">To ask about a proposal or withdraw one, <a href="{{ '/data/' | url }}#contact">contact us</a>.</p>
  {% else %}
  <div class="notice">
    <p class="notice__eyebrow">Not open yet</p>
    <p>
      The proposal form is not open yet. In the meantime,
      <a href="{{ '/data/' | url }}#contact">contact us</a> with the speaker&rsquo;s details and a
      volunteer from the Editorial Board will pick them up.
    </p>
  </div>
  {% endif %}
</section>
